  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The work done in a cyclic process is equal to the area of closed P-V curve cycle.</p><p>Work done,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;Area of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p><p>In the given P-V graph, the process is clockwise. So, the work done will be positive which means that the system is doing the work.</p>"
  }
